  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/55CB7B">Definition <span data-tag="55CB7B">1.2.12.3</span>.</a>strongly final Let $\calC $ be a simplicial set. A vertex $X$ of $\calC $ is <em>strongly final</em> if the projection $\calC _{/X} \rightarrow \calC $ is a trivial fibration of simplicial sets. </p>
